```

What does this print?

```javascript
const m = new Map();
m.set("1", "a");
m.set(1, "b");
const o = {};
o["1"] = "a";
o[1] = "b";
console.log(m.size, Object.keys(o).length);
```

What does this print? Write it as Node shows an array, for example `[ 1, 2, 3 ]`.

```javascript
function* naturals() {
  let n = 1;
  while (true) yield n++;
}
console.log(naturals().map((n) => n * 3).filter((n) => n % 2 === 0).take(3).toArray());
```
